.TH APSIS 1 "2026-09-29" "apsis 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.\" No hyphenation: action names and paths must stay whole.
.nh
.SH NAME
apsis \- simple system snapshots and file restore for the COSMIC desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apsis
.br
.B apsis
.B \-\-window
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apsis
is a panel applet for the COSMIC desktop that creates, lists, deletes and browses rsync
system snapshots on a backup disk, and restores single files from them.
Its popup looks like a small terminal and follows the COSMIC theme.
.PP
Snapshots are kept in Timeshift's on\-disk layout
.RI ( timeshift/snapshots/<name>/
on the backup disk), so snapshots Timeshift made are listed, browsed, restored from and
deleted like Apsis's own.
Apsis doesn't need or run Timeshift.
It is manual only: there is no schedule, and a snapshot is only deleted when the user deletes
it.
Encrypted (LUKS) backup disks aren't supported yet.
.PP
Started by the COSMIC panel,
.B apsis
is a panel button that opens the popup.
Started anywhere else (the app launcher, a terminal), or with
.BR \-\-window ,
it shows the same view in a normal window.
.PP
Everything that needs root (listing, creating, deleting, browsing, restoring, writing the
settings) goes through
.BR apsis\-helper ,
a small system service started on demand over D\-Bus, and polkit asks for the password.
Apsis doesn't work without it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-window
Show the popup's view in a normal, resizable window, even when started by the panel.
Esc closes the window.
.SH KEYS
Every
.B [key]
hint at the bottom of the view is also a button.
.B ?
shows these keys inside Apsis.
.SS Snapshot list
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", " Up ", " Down ", " Home ", " End
Move the selection.
.TP
.B c
Create a snapshot; type a comment at the
.B >
line, then Enter.
rsync runs at idle I/O priority and nice 19.
.TP
.B d
Delete the marked snapshots, or the selected one if none are marked; type
.B y
and Enter to confirm.
Marked snapshots are deleted one at a time, and the delete stops at the first failure.
.TP
.B space
Mark or unmark the selected snapshot for deletion.
.TP
.B J
Mark or unmark, then move down.
.TP
.B p
Prune: show which old snapshots
.B keep
would delete, and delete them after
.B y
and Enter.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the list.
.TP
.B Enter
Browse the selected snapshot's files.
.TP
.B Tab
Make the details pane active, and back.
.TP
.B s
Settings (see
.BR SETTINGS ).
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel the prompt, go back, clear the marks, then close.
.SS Snapshot browser
.TP
.BR Enter ", " l
Into the selected folder.
.TP
.BR Backspace ", " h
Up one folder.
.TP
.B space
Mark or unmark for restoring.
.TP
.B J
Mark or unmark, then move down.
.TP
.B R
Restore the marked entries (or the selected one): to a folder under
.I ~/Apsis-restored
or back to their original place.
A dry run shows the plan first; Enter runs it.
.TP
.B r
Read the folder again.
.SS Settings
.TP
.B space
Change the selected row.
.TP
.BR + ", " \- ", " e
One more, one fewer, or type the number (keep, remind).
.TP
.BR a ", " x
Add a filter, remove the selected filter.
.TP
.B w
Write the settings (password asked).
.TP
.B r
Read them again, dropping changes.
.SH SETTINGS
The backup device and filters are Apsis's config,
.IR /etc/apsis/config.toml ,
written by
.B apsis\-helper
when
.B w
is pressed.
Before it exists, the settings show what was read from Timeshift's
.I /etc/timeshift/timeshift.json
(the backup device and filter list; the file is only read), and
.B w
saves that as Apsis's own.
.TP
.B device
The disk or partition snapshots go to: a Linux filesystem, not encrypted.
Prefer another disk than the system one.
.TP
.B home
Per user:
.B excluded
(nothing from the home folder, the default),
.B hidden files only
(dot\-files and dot\-folders, i.e. settings), or
.B everything
(all files).
Kept as Timeshift's patterns in the filter list.
.TP
.B filters
rsync patterns: plain ones exclude, a leading
.RB \(dq +
\(dq includes, and the first match wins.
.B *
matches within one folder level,
.B **
across folders, and a leading
.B /
starts at the root.
For example
.I /var/lib/libvirt/**
leaves out virtual machine images.
Built\-in excludes (caches, /proc, /tmp, other mounts) are always added.
.TP
.B apsis keep
Per user, saved at once; off by default.
Keeps the newest N snapshots without a comment
(commented ones are pinned: kept, and not counted);
.B p
previews and, after
.BR y ,
deletes the older ones.
The newest snapshot is never deleted.
.TP
.B apsis remind
Per user, saved at once.
The panel icon turns the warning colour when the newest snapshot is older than this many
days (default 7; 0 turns it off).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apsis/config.toml
Apsis's config: the backup device's UUID and the filters.
Written only by
.BR apsis\-helper ,
0644, owned by root; the previous file is kept as
.IR config.toml.bak .
.TP
.I /etc/timeshift/timeshift.json
Timeshift's settings, read once for the import while there is no
.IR config.toml ;
never written.
.TP
.I ~/Apsis-restored/<snapshot>/
Where folder\-mode restores go, owned by the user.
Original\-mode restores keep each replaced file as
.IR <name>.apsis-before-<snapshot> .
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/apsis-helper
The privileged helper.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system-services/io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.Helper.service
.TQ
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.Helper.conf
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/apsis-helper.service
D\-Bus activation, bus policy and systemd unit of the helper.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.policy
The polkit actions below.
.SH SECURITY
The applet runs as the user and never as root.
.B apsis\-helper
checks each call with polkit, against the caller's D\-Bus name, and runs one operation at a
time.
It mounts the backup disk (by UUID, nosuid, nodev) for the length of one call, read\-only
except for a create or a delete.
A delete only removes a folder named like a snapshot under
.IR timeshift/snapshots/ ,
reached without any symlink, with an
.IR info.json ,
and with nothing mounted inside it; it never follows a symlink or crosses into another
filesystem, and then removes only that snapshot's tag links.
Calls and results are logged to the journal
.RB ( "journalctl \-u apsis\-helper" ).
For the active session:
.TP
.B io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.list
Listing snapshots and reading the settings: no password.
.TP
.B io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.create
.TQ
.B io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.delete
.TQ
.B io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.configure
.TQ
.B io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.browse
.TQ
.B io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.restore
Creating, deleting, writing the settings, browsing and folder\-mode restores: the password,
remembered for a few minutes
.RB ( auth_admin_keep ).
.TP
.B io.github.atraxsrc.Apsis.restore-original
Restoring files over the running system: the password every time
.RB ( auth_admin ).
.PP
Inactive and remote sessions need the password for every action.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR polkit (8),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR timeshift (1)
.PP
